<title>JORDAN: Jordan buys 50,000 T U.S. yellow corn.</title>
<headline>Jordan buys 50,000 T U.S. yellow corn.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan bought 50,000 tonnes of U.S. number 3 corn or better in one lot at $154.25 per tonne C and F, for first half November shipment, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Jordan's Ministry of Supply made the purchase from Geneva based Romak, traders said.</p>
<p>Jordan has an annual consumption of yellow corn of 400,000 to 500,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Amman Bureau 9626+623776</p>
